  "thread_id": 1627444860,
  "subject": "[AMBER] questions about unbond parameters",
  "messages": [
    {
      "message_id": 1627444860,
      "author": "������",
      "date_raw": "Wed, 28 Jul 2021 12:01:00 +0800 (CST)",
      "body": "Hello,I am a user of AMBER.When I read unbond parameters in parm10.dat,I found that there are only few atom parameters(as seen in the picture attached),while there are many common used atoms don't have the unbond parameters(such as CA CB and so on).Therefore,I want to know where is those atoms' unbond parameters?And if I add \"CA        1  0.08             \" in the unbond parameters regions in parm10.dat,what will happen?Will the CA atoms adopt my LJ parameters(1,0.08)?Thanks so much.\nLooking forward to your response!",
      "url": "http://archive.ambermd.org/202107/0228.html"
    },
    {
      "message_id": 1627472420,
      "author": "David A Case",
      "date_raw": "Wed, 28 Jul 2021 07:40:20 -0400",
      "body": "On Wed, Jul 28, 2021, 李政新 wrote:\n>Hello,I am a user of AMBER.When I read unbond parameters in parm10.dat,I\n>found that there are only few atom parameters(as seen in the picture\n>attached),while there are many common used atoms don't have the unbond\n>parameters(such as CA CB and so on).Therefore,I want to know where is those\n>atoms' unbond parameters?\nThe identifiers you see are atom types, not atom names.  You can find the\natom types by looking in the .lib file you loaded, or by using parmed (look\nat the printLJTypes and changeLJSingleType commands, plus related ones.)\nWe recommend that you create a frcmod file if you want to change parameters:\nthis is easier to document then editing parm10.dat itself.\n...good luck....dac",
      "url": "http://archive.ambermd.org/202107/0231.html",
      "in_reply_to": 1627444860
    },
    {
      "message_id": 1627518830,
      "author": "������",
      "date_raw": "Thu, 29 Jul 2021 08:33:50 +0800 (CST)",
      "body": "Thanks for your advice.Sorry to have another question that I still can not find the unbond parameters for lots of atom names(or atom types) in the parm.dat or .lib.Where are those unbond parameters,please?\n----- ԭʼ�ʼ� -----\n������: \"David A Case\" <dacase.chem.rutgers.edu>\n�ռ���: \"amber\" <amber.ambermd.\norg>\n����ʱ��: ������, 2021�� 7 �� 28�� ���� 7:40:20\n����: Re: [AMBER] questions about unbond parameters\nOn Wed, Jul 28, 2021, ������ wrote:\n>Hello,I am a user of AMBER.When I read unbond parameters in parm10.dat,I\n>found that there are only few atom parameters(as seen in the picture\n>attached),while there are many common used atoms don't have the unbond\n>parameters(such as CA CB and so on).Therefore,I want to know where is those\n>atoms' unbond parameters?\nThe identifiers you see are atom types, not atom names.  You can find the\natom types by looking in the .lib file you loaded, or by using parmed (look\nat the printLJTypes and changeLJSingleType commands, plus related ones.)\nWe recommend that you create a frcmod file if you want to change parameters:\nthis is easier to document then editing parm10.dat itself.\n...good luck....dac",
      "url": "http://archive.ambermd.org/202107/0237.html",
      "in_reply_to": 1627444860
    },
    {
      "message_id": 1627559682,
      "author": "David A Case",
      "date_raw": "Thu, 29 Jul 2021 07:54:42 -0400",
      "body": "On Thu, Jul 29, 2021, 李政新 wrote:\n>Thanks for your advice.Sorry to have another question that I still can not\n>find the unbond parameters for lots of atom names(or atom types) in the\n>parm.dat or .lib.Where are those unbond parameters,please?\nCan you provide an example of a parameter you cannot find?  If you are\nloading several parm files (using LoadAmberParams), you may need to look in\nall of them.\n....dac",
      "url": "http://archive.ambermd.org/202107/0238.html",
